<Title>Typography</Title>

NeoMateria uses a three-strategy system for handling text that exceeds its container. Every text element applies **at least one strategy** depending on whether the element is UI chrome (navigation, labels) or content (cards, panels).

---

## Strategy 1 — Single-line truncation

**When to use:** UI chrome elements where wrapping would break layout — navigation labels, table cells, compact list items.

```css
.Element-label {
  overflow: hidden;
  text-overflow: ellipsis;
  white-space: nowrap;
}
```

**Applied to:** `NeoNavItem` labels.

<div style={{ padding: '16px' }}>
	<div
		style={{
			border: '1px solid var(--docs-color-border)',
			borderRadius: '8px',
			display: 'flex',
			flexDirection: 'column',
			gap: '4px',
			inlineSize: '220px',
			padding: '8px',
		}}
	>
		{[
			'Short label',
			'A slightly longer navigation label',
			'An extremely long navigation label that would normally wrap onto a second line',
		].map((label) => (
			<div
				key={label}
				style={{
					borderRadius: '6px',
					color: 'var(--docs-color-text-label)',
					fontSize: '0.875rem',
					overflow: 'hidden',
					padding: '6px 10px',
					textOverflow: 'ellipsis',
					whiteSpace: 'nowrap',
				}}
			>
				{label}
			</div>
		))}
	</div>
</div>

---

## Strategy 2 — Line clamp

**When to use:** Content previews where the element has a fixed role — card titles, card descriptions, panel titles.

```css
.Element-title {
  display: -webkit-box;
  -webkit-box-orient: vertical;
  -webkit-line-clamp: var(--Element-sizing-titleClamp);
  line-clamp: var(--Element-sizing-titleClamp);
  overflow: hidden;
}
```

The clamp count is exposed as a CSS variable so consumers can override it without a prop:

```css
.my-context .NeoCard {
  --NeoCard-sizing-titleClamp: 1;
  --NeoCard-sizing-descriptionClamp: 2;
}
```

**Applied to:** `NeoCard` title (2 lines), `NeoCard` description (3 lines), `NeoProgressPanel` title (2 lines).

<div
	style={{
		display: 'grid',
		gap: '24px',
		gridTemplateColumns: 'repeat(auto-fill, minmax(240px, 1fr))',
		padding: '16px',
	}}
>
	{[
		{
			label: 'Short title — no clamp',
			title: 'A Normal Card Title',
			clamp: 2,
		},
		{
			label: 'Long title — clamped at 2 lines',
			title: 'An Extraordinarily Long Title That Will Be Clamped After Two Lines Because It Just Keeps Going',
			clamp: 2,
		},
		{
			label: 'Long description — clamped at 3 lines',
			title: 'Normal Title',
			description: 'This is a very long description that goes well beyond three lines of text. It demonstrates how the line-clamp strategy cuts off content cleanly with an ellipsis after the configured number of lines, keeping the card height consistent regardless of how much text is provided by the consumer.',
			clamp: 3,
		},
	].map((card) => (
		<div key={card.label} style={{ display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column', gap: '8px' }}>
			<p style={{ color: 'var(--docs-color-text-secondary)', fontSize: '0.75rem', margin: '0' }}>
				{card.label}
			</p>
			<div
				style={{
					border: '1px solid var(--docs-color-border)',
					borderRadius: '8px',
					overflow: 'hidden',
				}}
			>
				<div style={{ background: 'var(--neo-color-blue100)', blockSize: '120px' }} />
				<div style={{ padding: '12px' }}>
					<p
						style={{
							WebkitBoxOrient: 'vertical',
							WebkitLineClamp: 2,
							display: '-webkit-box',
							fontWeight: '600',
							lineHeight: '1.3',
							margin: '0 0 6px',
							overflow: 'hidden',
						}}
					>
						{card.title}
					</p>
					{card.description && (
						<p
							style={{
								WebkitBoxOrient: 'vertical',
								WebkitLineClamp: card.clamp,
								color: 'var(--docs-color-text-secondary)',
								display: '-webkit-box',
								fontSize: '0.875rem',
								lineHeight: '1.5',
								margin: '0',
								overflow: 'hidden',
							}}
						>
							{card.description}
						</p>
					)}
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	))}
</div>

---

## Strategy 3 — Overflow wrap + hyphenation

**When to use:** All multi-line text as a baseline safety net. Prevents a single long word or URL from causing horizontal overflow without restricting line count.

```css
.Element {
  hyphens: auto;
  overflow-wrap: break-word;
}
```

**`hyphens: auto` requires a `lang` attribute** on the element or an ancestor — typically `<html lang="de">`. Without it the property has no effect and `overflow-wrap` acts as a fallback. This is by design: the component sets the capability, the app provides the language context.

```html
<!-- app root — enables hyphenation for all components -->
<html lang="de">

<!-- or per-section -->
<section lang="de">
  <NeoCard title="Donaudampfschifffahrtsgesellschaft" ... />
</section>
```

**Applied to:** `NeoButton`, `NeoCard`, `NeoProgressPanel`, and all other multi-line text elements as a baseline.

### Hyphenation demo

Both boxes use `overflow-wrap: break-word` and `hyphens: auto`. Only the one with `lang="de"` produces proper German hyphenation.

> **In your app:** set `lang="de"` on `<html>` or the nearest relevant ancestor. NeoMateria components declare `hyphens: auto` — the browser does the rest.

